    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but like if a government actually has to make a choice... if they have to pick between keeping energy prices low and stable for workers right now vs. hitting those aggressive carbon targets to stop climate change, which one is the more responsible path to take? like, isn't it basically more important to prevent a global climate catastrophe than to worry about temporary economic spikes?",
